          "sourcePage": 59,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 4, lower-left triangle",
          "description": "Unshaded triangle with A at the lower left, B above and slightly right of A, and C to the right at an intermediate height. Mid-segment arrows indicate A to B and B to C; AC has no arrow.",
          "mathematics": "AB = 2a + b; BC = a − 3b. The triangle law gives AC = AB + BC.",
          "answerVisibility": "Only supplied vector labels are visible."
        },
        "derived": false,
